   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-02-18">February 18, 1942</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>,</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>Several weeks ago <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1141" type="person">Trude</rs> gave me
               a copy of your pamphlet <unclear>on</unclear>
               <q>War Aims</q> which only tonight have I had a chance to read. I want to
                  <unclear>hasten</unclear> to express my profound agreement with its views.</p>
            <p>Unless we stand up now and are <unclear>counted</unclear> for the New Deal, the war will in a true sense be
               lost, for we will be <unclear>reverting</unclear> to or perpetuating conditions that make inevitable the future growth of
               reaction, militarism and nationalism. Unless we appeal now to the underground liberation
               movements in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__736" type="place">Europe</rs> and utilize the
               anti-fascist-<unclear>emigre</unclear> groups, our hopes of European federation will be defeated. But
               there is no need to harangue you on this subject!</p>
            <p>How to make such a view politically effective – that is the question. Your pamphlet
               is, I feel, a real contribution.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4095" type="person"
                  >Jospeh Lash</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
